+// ── P1 fp32-EPILOGUE FUSION (perf-lever #1; .perf/perf_lever_impl_design.json).
+//    Folds the inter-GEMM scalar epilogue post-loops in dectc_forward_tile into
+//    the GEMM out() lambda (relocates the per-element add/gelu/round to WG0's
+//    fragment-decode after wgmma_wait_group<0> drains — NO reduction-order
+//    change, the fp32 accumulator the lambda receives is the SAME value the
+//    standalone fp32-output store wrote). The maxed tc_gemm_block_unpipelined
+//    engine is REUSED unchanged; only the out() accessor differs.
+//
+//    SG_TUNED_DEC_EPI_FUSE (0/1): MASTER enable. 0 (DEFAULT, revert-safe) → the
+//      original standalone GEMM + separate epilogue post-loops run unchanged →
+//      BYTE-IDENTICAL PTX to every shipped build (sha256-verified, same compile
+//      path). 1 → the two folds below are active (each still independently
+//      gateable via its sub-knob).
+//
+//    TWO INDEPENDENT FOLDS (each defaults to the master but overrides alone, so a
+//    fold-A gate-RED reverts A and KEEPS B: -DSG_TUNED_DEC_EPI_FUSE=1
+//    -DSG_TUNED_DEC_EPI_FUSE_A=0):
+//      • FOLD B — SG_TUNED_DEC_EPI_FUSE_B: ff0_b + dec_gelu + X_gact (the ff0
+//        epilogue, sites ~1572-1577). BYTE-IDENTICAL transport-only: the fwd-f32
+//        GEMM (dectc_gemm_fwd_f32) already emits the exact fp32 wgmma accumulator
+//        v; pre = v + ff0_b[j] is the SAME fp32 add, only relocated into the
+//        lambda — the ff0pre bf16 round and the gelu→X_gact bf16 round are
+//        bit-for-bit the post-loop's (no atomics, CTA-local fragment order, the
+//        sc.work materialization is NOT relied upon — but sc.work IS still written
+//        below for the bwd; see the wrapper). LN reduce sc.work UNTOUCHED.
+//      • FOLD A — SG_TUNED_DEC_EPI_FUSE_A: in_b qkv-bias (the in_proj epilogue,
+//        sites ~1534-1538). A sub-bf16-ULP single-vs-double-round CHANGE:
+//        shipping path is bf16(bf16(x@w^T) + in_b) (double round); the fold makes
+//        it bf16(x@w^T_fp32 + in_b) (single round) — the ABSORBABLE direction
